  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self'">
  <title>Theme Picker</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="theme-picker.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="theme-controls">
    <button data-theme-toggle data-theme="light" aria-pressed="true" aria-label="Switch to light theme">
      Light
    </button>
    <button data-theme-toggle data-theme="dark" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Switch to dark theme">
      Dark
    </button>
  </div>

  <script src="theme-picker.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

**Security notes:**
- Theme preference is non-sensitive UI state, so `localStorage` is acceptable per §1 (no tokens, keys, or PII stored)
- All user input is validated against a strict allowlist (`VALID_THEMES`)
- CSP is set to restrict script sources to self only
- No external resources or remote content loaded
- DOM manipulation is minimal and uses safe methods (no `innerHTML` with user input)
